# Shell scripts must check out with LF, on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf is on for the people working on this repository, which is right
# for the Windows tooling and wrong for anything that runs in Linux. The
# scripts under infra/scripts are shipped INTO a container: migrate-data.sh
# base64-encodes infra/scripts/migration/*.sh and hands the result to `bash`
# inside a Fargate task. A file that checked out with CRLF arrives there with a
# carriage return on the shebang line and fails as "bad interpreter", during
# the cutover window, on the step that moves the database.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are consumed by Linux runners and by Terraform.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.tf text eol=lf
